WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.400
Good morning , John, it's Friday.

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.450
So we've been doing this stuff for eight years
now on You--hello there.

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.450
Hi.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.450
Corndog.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.450
Hi.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.450
Ahmm.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.450
Yaahh.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.519
Why are you--haaah.

00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:14.990
Hm.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.450
AAHH.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.920
Okay.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.830
That was weird.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:30.800
I um--I was--aaaaaaah!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.260
[sighs]

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.579
The universe apparently wants me to do something
not in this chair and with these books.

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:40.579
[music plays]

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:41.579
1, 2, 1, 2, 3, 4...

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:42.579
Arrrghhhh!

00:00:42.579 --> 00:01:06.680
I remember when I was a young man, my momma
took me to the store--

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.700
125 cm.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.499
But no reason to stop there!

00:01:09.499 --> 00:01:14.670
--my pants are too bright, too dark, too baggy,
too light--

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.539
Aughhh, auh, auh, auhhhh.

00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:19.359
--whatever you choose will be right.

00:01:19.359 --> 00:01:25.459
155 cm, everybody, 155 cm, now let's go for
another level, because you can't build a giant

00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:28.020
tower and just leave it there.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.219
You have to see how far you can go.

00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:31.990
and the first time I read Thoreau--

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:37.369
Okay, Book of Merlin is on, which opens up
the opportunity for another thing to get stacked

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.369
on here.

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:39.609
It doesn't mean anything.

00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:41.020
Let's go with this.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:48.299
That I try not to say too much just with my
clothes.

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:49.299
Ohhhh!

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:50.639
Well, it had to happen.

00:01:50.639 --> 00:01:53.749
The question is, can ya beat me?

00:01:53.749 --> 00:01:58.770
So first I wanna apologize for the amount
of underwear that I showed while constructing

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.770
my book tower.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:03.659
That was both unintentional and embarrassing
but I'm certainly not gonna go rebuild an

00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:07.279
entire book tower just so I can go put on
a belt and do it so that you don't see the

00:02:07.279 --> 00:02:08.799
clothes that happen to cover up my bottom.

00:02:08.799 --> 00:02:13.080
Second, I made a book tower that was 155cm
tall, and I believe that that is not as tall

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.280
as a book tower can be, so I would like you
to beat me.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:21.730
The five highest towers and the five most
stylin' towers will win a special gift package

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.590
sent directly to your house from me.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.519
Rules: You cannot use any kind of adhesive
or clamps or anything that binds the books

00:02:27.519 --> 00:02:28.519
together.

00:02:28.519 --> 00:02:29.599
It has to be composed of loose books.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:33.349
Rule number two: You cannot hurt yourself
or do anything that might cause you to hurt

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:34.349
yourself please.

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:37.530
Three: You can only use books, but you can
pool together books from multiple sources.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.629
Four: You have to have a tape measure and
you have to measure in centimeters because

00:02:40.629 --> 00:02:44.730
inches are dumb and I cannot believe that
we still use any kind of measurement system

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.310
that is not based on the numerical system
that we use of base-10.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.970
Base-12?

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.500
Why are there 12 inches in a foot?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.730
To enter, send a picture of your book tower,
with the subject 'Book Tower' and then the

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.040
height of your book tower in the subject line
to hankandjohn@gmail.com.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.609
And lastly, it is time for the Nerdfighteria
Census.

00:03:02.609 --> 00:03:06.400
This'll be the third annual, we've been doing
it since 2013, and the idea is just so that

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.550
the community can get to know itself better,
know what it is, know who it is, I can do

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.790
an analysis, know what you want from this.

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.900
We can better plan any future tour that we
might do so that we know where people are,

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.819
and this year, for the first time, we actually
talked to some researchers who are doing some

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:27.870
science and we had them put in a few questions
which will help them better understand the

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.650
world and the people in it, so that's cool.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.870
It's not an insignificant thing, it takes
a little while to do, like 10-30 minutes,

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:37.760
but we really appreciate it when people do
do that, and there's a link in the description

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.569
if you wanna go and do it, so thank you, we
appreciate that.

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:44.680
Looking forward to seeing all your book towers
and, John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

